      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I also think it would be good to be able to get some bool for if the keyboard is open at all (searching for world/user, using input field, using chatbox, etc).\n\nThis is because sometimes I use Input.GetKeyDown for desktop inputs. But often, I don't actually want to make these key presses do things when VRC Keyboard has focus.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-17T10:29:16.667Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Now that you can click on an InputField to open VRChat's keyboard, there should be a way to force the keyboard to close through Udon.\n\nFor example, in a game world I am working on, users have a limited time to type text into an Input Field. When the time runs out, I want to close the VRChat keyboard if it was opened, by calling something along the lines of \"VRChatKeyboard.CloseKeyboard();\".",
